## A1[Write Frontend] --> A2[HLC Generator]

When a client submits a write through the REST API, the request first lands on the **Write Frontend** (`A1`). The frontend is a thin Spring MVC controller whose sole responsibility is to translate the HTTP payload into a domain command and hand it off to the **Hybrid Logical Clock (HLC) Generator** (`A2`). The HLC generator is a stateless component that stamps every command with a causally‑consistent timestamp before it is persisted or replicated.  
Below is a step‑by‑step walk‑through of the flow, the domain model, and the supporting infrastructure.

### 1. Domain Model (LLD)

```java
interface KeyValueCommand {
    String getKey();
    Object getValue();
    HLC getTimestamp();
}

