### Architecture pattern – resilient event publishing

The `CrdtService` that persists the `CrdtEvent` to Kafka is wrapped in a Resilience4j circuit‑breaker. If the broker stalls, the breaker opens, queues the event locally, and retries once the circuit closes, guaranteeing *at‑least‑once* delivery without blocking the write path.

    @Service
    public class CrdtService {
        private final KafkaTemplate<String, CrdtEvent> kafka;
        private final CircuitBreaker breaker = CircuitBreaker.ofDefaults("kafkaBreaker");

        public void publish(CrdtEvent ev) {
            Supplier<Void> publisher = () -> { kafka.send("crdt-topic", ev.getId(), ev); return null; };
            Try.ofSupplier(breaker.decorateSupplier(publisher))
               .recover(throwable -> { /* fallback to local buffer */ return null; })
               .get();
        }
    }

