## A3 --> A4[Local Replica Store]

The local replica store is the heart of the multi‑master geo‑replication pipeline. It accepts HLC‑tagged CRDT updates from the **A3** write‑handler, persists them, and serves read requests with linearizable guarantees. The store is designed to be pluggable, fault‑tolerant, and to expose a clean REST API for client access.

### LLD – Java Domain Model

```java
// Domain contracts
public interface KeyValueStore {
    void put(String key, CrdtValue value, HlcStamp stamp);
    CrdtValue get(String key);
    void delete(String key, HlcStamp stamp);
}

public interface CrdtValue {
    CrdtValue merge(CrdtValue other);
    boolean isConflicting(CrdtValue other);
}

// Core abstractions
public abstract class AbstractStore implements KeyValueStore {
    protected final Map<String, StoredEntry> storage = new ConcurrentHashMap<>();
    protected final Logger log = LoggerFactory.getLogger(getClass());

    protected static class StoredEntry {
        final CrdtValue value;
        final HlcStamp stamp;
        StoredEntry(CrdtValue v, HlcStamp s) { this.value = v; this.stamp = s; }
    }
}

// Concrete implementation
public class InMemoryStore extends AbstractStore {
    @Override
    public void put(String key, CrdtValue value, HlcStamp stamp) {
        storage.merge(key, new StoredEntry(value, stamp),
            (old, newE) -> newE.stamp.compareTo(old.stamp) > 0 ? newE : old);
    }
    @Override public CrdtValue get(String key) { return storage.getOrDefault(key, null).value; }
    @Override public void delete(String key, HlcStamp stamp) {
        storage.computeIfPresent(key, (k, old) ->
            stamp.compareTo(old.stamp) > 0 ? null : old);
    }
}
```

