## B2 --> B3[CRDT Engine]

The CRDT engine is the heart of the geo‑replicated KV store, turning causally‑ordered HLC timestamps into deterministic, convergent state. It exposes a *merge* contract that guarantees that, regardless of the order in which replicas receive updates, the resulting value is the same. The engine is implemented as a pluggable `CRDT` interface, with concrete types for common data structures (GCounter, ORSet, LWW-Register). The Java domain model below shows the core abstraction and a simple `GCounter` implementation that is used by the write‑frontend.

```java
public interface CRDT<T> {
    T merge(T other);
    T value();
}

public abstract class AbstractCRDT<T> implements CRDT<T> {
    protected T state;
    public AbstractCRDT(T initial) { this.state = initial; }
    @Override public T value() { return state; }
}

public class GCounter extends AbstractCRDT<Long> {
    public GCounter() { super(0L); }
    public void increment(long delta) { state += delta; }
    @Override public Long merge(Long other) { return Math.max(state, other); }
}

public enum CRDTType { GCOUNTER, ORSET, LWW }
```

