## B4 – Replicate (HLC)

The *Replicate* phase is the heart of the causal‑consistency engine. It takes an incoming write, stamps it with a Hybrid Logical Clock (HLC) timestamp, publishes the event to Kafka, and guarantees that every replica receives the event in a causally‑consistent order. The design hinges on three orthogonal layers:

1. **Domain model** – a clean OOP hierarchy that encapsulates the HLC logic, CRDT state, and replication contract.  
2. **Transport layer** – Spring Kafka producers/consumers wired through Resilience4j for fault tolerance and Axon for event‑driven command handling.  
3. **REST façade** – a lightweight Spring MVC controller that accepts client writes, delegates to the command bus, and returns the optimistic HLC‑tagged response.

Below is a concise, but complete, Java implementation of these layers.

```java
// Domain layer – HLC abstraction
public interface HLC {
    long getPhysical();   // epoch millis
    long getLogical();    // logical counter
    HLC tick();           // advance timestamp
    HLC merge(HLC other); // causal merge
}

// Concrete implementation
public final class HybridLogicalClock implements HLC {
    private final long physical;
    private final long logical;

    public HybridLogicalClock(long physical, long logical) {
        this.physical = physical;
        this.logical = logical;
    }

    @Override
    public long getPhysical() { return physical; }

    @Override
    public long getLogical() { return logical; }

    @Override
    public HLC tick() {
        long now = System.currentTimeMillis();
        long newLogical = (now > physical) ? 0 : logical + 1;
        return new HybridLogicalClock(now, newLogical);
    }

    @Override
    public HLC merge(HLC other) {
        long maxPhysical = Math.max(physical, other.getPhysical());
        long maxLogical = (maxPhysical == physical && maxPhysical == other.getPhysical())
                ? Math.max(logical, other.getLogical())
                : 0;
        return new HybridLogicalClock(maxPhysical, maxLogical);
    }
}

// CRDT state interface
public interface CRDT<K, V> {
    void apply(K key, V value, HLC ts);
    V read(K key);
}

// Example: LWW-Register
public final class LWWRegister implements CRDT<String, String> {
    private final Map<String, Pair<String, HLC>> store = new ConcurrentHashMap<>();

    @Override
    public void apply(String key, String value, HLC ts) {
        store.merge(key, new Pair<>(value, ts), (old, newVal) ->
                (newVal.getSecond().compareTo(old.getSecond()) > 0) ? newVal : old);
    }

    @Override
    public String read(String key) {
        return store.getOrDefault(key, new Pair<>(null, null)).getFirst();
    }
}

// Command object
public record WriteCommand(String key, String value, HLC ts) {}

// Axon command handler
@Component
public class WriteHandler {
    private final CRDT<String, String> crdt;

    public WriteHandler(CRDT<String, String> crdt) { this.crdt = crdt; }

    @CommandHandler
    public void handle(WriteCommand cmd) {
        crdt.apply(cmd.key(), cmd.value(), cmd.ts());
    }
}
```

