**Solution 1 – Merge Two Sorted Lists (Iterative)**  

    public ListNode mergeSorted(ListNode a, ListNode b) {
        ListNode dummy = new ListNode(0);
        ListNode tail = dummy;
        while (a != null && b != null) {
            if (a.val <= b.val) {
                tail.next = a; a = a.next;
            } else {
                tail.next = b; b = b.next;
            }
            tail = tail.next;
        }
        tail.next = (a != null) ? a : b;
        return dummy.next;
    }

**Solution 2 – K‑th Smallest in G‑Counter Merge**  

    public long kthSmallestGCounter(List<GCounterEntry> entries, int k) {
        PriorityQueue<Long> heap = new PriorityQueue<>(Comparator.reverseOrder());
        for (GCounterEntry e : entries) {
            heap.offer(e.getCount());
            if (heap.size() > k) heap.poll();
        }
        return heap.peek();
    }

