### High‑Level Narrative (no fenced code)

The system receives a client request, creates a CRDT update stamped with an HLC, stores it locally, and publishes it to Kafka. Each replica consumes the topic, verifies causal order via the HLC, and merges the CRDT. If a node is temporarily unreachable, the circuit breaker opens, buffering events until connectivity resumes. Acknowledgements flow back through a separate topic, enabling the sender to clean its pending queue. This flow ensures eventual consistency while preserving causality across data centers.

